            <ArticleTitle>[Has the classic chordotomy a future? (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>379-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Evaluating our results of anterior-lateral chordotomy in 88 patients suffering from intractable pain, we can state that this is a useful surgical procedure. Today however it has to be replaced by the so-called percutaneous cervical chordotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
